Project Mu: Kage, Mu's private window

Incognito is called Kage (影, shadow) in Mu's interface (the strings are
renamed by build.py gen); this patch gives it Mu's look and protection.

  * uBlock Origin Lite, when installed (patch 0007 loads mu\ublock), is
    allowed in Kage windows: "Allow in Incognito" is turned on once, the
    first time it loads, through the same helper as the Extensions page.
  * Kage windows get Mu's ink instead of Chromium's grey: themes do not
    apply to private windows, so the system colours behind the frame,
    toolbar and address bar are set to sumi tones, a step darker than a
    normal Mu window. Only dark, greyscale, unthemed windows are affected,
    which in Mu means private windows only.
  * The Kage New Tab page: sumi background, washi text, Mu's display face
    for the heading, and the cookie-controls card in kiri with an inkan
    edge. The splash and tab icons (branding/ overlay) are an inkan ensō
    around 影 and a ring half in shadow.

diff --git a/chrome/browser/extensions/extension_service.cc b/chrome/browser/extensions/extension_service.cc
index 43df9e2..fc2a7d1 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/extensions/extension_service.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/extensions/extension_service.cc
@@ -90,6 +90,7 @@
 #include "extensions/browser/extension_registrar.h"
 #include "extensions/browser/extension_registry.h"
 #include "extensions/browser/extension_system.h"
+#include "chrome/browser/extensions/extension_util.h"
 #include "extensions/browser/extension_util.h"
 #include "extensions/browser/extensions_browser_client.h"
 #include "extensions/browser/external_install_info.h"
@@ -404,6 +405,13 @@ void ExtensionService::Init() {
           extension_prefs_->UpdateExtensionPref(extension_id, "ack_ntp_bubble",
                                                 base::Value(true));
         }
+        // Project Mu: the content blocker protects private (Kage) windows
+        // too. Turn on "Allow in Incognito" once; the helper reloads it so
+        // the permission applies now, and later starts find it already on.
+        if (!extension_id.empty() && std::string_view(name) == "ublock" &&
+            !util::IsIncognitoEnabled(extension_id, profile_)) {
+          util::SetIsIncognitoEnabled(extension_id, profile_, true);
+        }
       }
     }
   }
